      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MISHIMA (14) needs a few scratchings to gain a start but if she fronts up she shapes as the one to beat. Much more consistent of late than most rivals here and only beaten 1-1/4 lengths the past two starts in races of more depth than this. KNOCK OF BEERS (6) missed the placings two starts back then ran a better race and finished 1.3 lengths away in fifth last time out over 1412m at Echuca. Has her share of ability. Hard to beat in this suitable race.  RIVAZZA (10) finished out of the money two starts back then she settled well back and was beaten 4.5 lengths when fifth in a 1300m contest at Bendigo two weeks ago. Beautifully placed and is sure to prove tough to beat. YAKI ISHI (5) campaigned in the NT during winter, placing on a couple of occasions, and will be better for the run back in Vic. Just needs luck from the gate. BELLAKAI (8) resumes, but has won first-up in the past and has done enough in a couple of recent jumpouts to suggest this is suitable option.",
